ause we we tell ourselves  a story why we can't be successful and  admitting the truth is too painful and  for me because I had an insane desire to  please people I think more was I didn't  want to let people down I don't like  what letting people down and so I'm  always careful what I what I commit to I  don't commit to something that I don't  follow through on I'm always early for  meetings I'm always early for connecting  with people I'm always you know earlier  on time I don't like letting people down  which is a great thing to have but the  flip side is you don't commit to people  you don't commit to projects that could  be really good for you that could help  you grow because you are afraid of  letting somebody down and so you don't  do the thing that you should do for me a  lot of it was meeting with people  meeting with entrepreneurs going and do  presentations I would secretly hope that  they would cancel on me because I felt  like maybe I'm not gonna add value here  you know I don't want to let them down  so three days before an event or the day  of a meeting I would secretly open my  email and hope that there would be a  cancellation notice I got okay I don't  have to go do that and it was a limiting  belief for me and once I recognized it  they know was able to attack it then I  was able to you know the trick to  overcoming these negative limiting  beliefs is one after the fact  understanding that I did it again I did  it again ah why did I do it again you're  so frustrated that you did it again that  you're playing small again that you said  no again when you really wanted to say  yes right you did it again you did it  again didn't just the awareness that's  more than half the battle because most  of the things that are holding you back  you're limiting self belief you don't  even know it's not even on your radar  you just do them so subconsciously  then you have zero awareness around them  and that is gonna forever hold you back  so just having that kind of awareness  after the fact is super important the  more you pick it up the more you keep  track of it the closer you will get to  the point of it happening to the point  where I am opening my email and secretly  hoping that that person is gonna cancel  and catching it right then and there it  doesn't happen right away but with time  right then and there and then having the  courage  take the action that you're supposed to  take that is best for you instead of  cowering down instead of doing what you  always do  instead of saying no and backing down  and saying no it's okay you know instead  of being that the lowest form version of  yourself instead of putting yourself  into this tiny box and mean this little  tiny person where you could be a lion  having the courage to go for it and the  more you pick it up the more frustrating  is gonna be to the point where you just  have to say yes and do it and again  every major breakthrough I've had in my  life and my business has come from me  crushing one of these limiting personal  beliefs so this videos a little longer  than I expected it to be but hopefully  is super valuable for you guys those are  my thoughts on the seven ways to develop  an unshakable belief in yourself I'm  curious to know what did you guys think  of the video did you like it do you  resonate with something what was the  most important thing that I said that  touched you leave it in the comments  below I want to join in the discussion  also did I miss it eight nine ten is  there something that you want to add to  this list to round it off leave it down  below super curious to see what you have  to say and finally I want to give a  shout out to Justin from sixty five  drums comm Justin thank you so much for  picking up a copy of my book really  means a lot to me thank you guys so much  for watching I believe in you I hope you  continue to believe in yourself and  whatever your one word is much love I'll  see you soon
 

